1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:08,861
This video shows the web player in plain JavaScript, with no framework. One call puts the animation on the page, and a few more control it.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,736
First, the player. It is one package from npm.

3
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,333
That adds the player to the project.

4
00:00:22,567 --> 00:00:25,519
Before any code, let's look at the page itself.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:40,696
It has an empty box with the id scene, a slider with the id progress, and four buttons. Jump and Play have ids too, and each speed button keeps its number in a data attribute.

6
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:43,665
Now, the script.

7
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,447
Let's create a player that fills the box.

8
00:00:56,267 --> 00:01:04,704
Create animator takes the address of the file and the element to fill. With nothing else, the file decides, so it starts on load and repeats forever.

9
00:01:05,933 --> 00:01:10,035
Next, the slider. Let's make it move the player to any moment.

10
00:01:23,733 --> 00:01:30,839
On every move, the player pauses, and set current progress moves it to that point, from zero to one.

11
00:01:32,067 --> 00:01:33,059
Let's drag it.

12
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:40,313
The ball follows the slider exactly.

13
00:01:41,533 --> 00:01:47,228
While the ball plays, the slider stays where it was. Let's make it follow the animation too.

14
00:02:01,167 --> 00:02:07,123
On every frame, get current progress reads where the player is, and the slider shows it.

15
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:14,696
Now the Jump and Play buttons. Jump goes to an exact time, and Play starts from there.

16
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:32,939
Set current time takes milliseconds, so five hundred is the bottom of the bounce. Play starts it from wherever it is.

17
00:02:34,167 --> 00:02:38,451
Let's stop it with the slider, jump to the bottom, and play from there.

18
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:49,439
The jump lands on the bottom of the bounce, and play carries on from there. The slider follows along.

19
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:54,951
Speed is one more call. Let's wire up the speed buttons.

20
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:13,995
Each speed button reads its number from its data attribute, and calls set playback rate with it.

21
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:18,316
Let's try double speed, and then half speed.

22
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:29,396
Twice as fast, then half as fast. The player keeps its place, and only the speed changes.

23
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:44,407
So, without any framework, one call creates the player, and a few more control it. Progress, time, play and speed each take one call. The web player guide in the docs lists every one of them.
